TASK (one change: move the stated cli-opencode default to llmgateway in the core docs):

FACTS (the operator decided this on 2026-10-21):
- The cli-opencode default model is now `llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash` (LLM Gateway, DevPass) on BOTH OpenCode versions.
- OpenCode 1 dispatches it as `--model llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash --variant max`. OpenCode 2 dispatches it as `-m llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash#max` (unchanged).
- Why: the opencode-go Go-plan quota is spent, so an OpenCode 1 dispatch on opencode-go hangs on "Go usage limit exceeded"; OpenCode 2 lists no opencode-go provider; one provider now serves both versions.
- `opencode-go` stays a documented, selectable provider with its models. Only the DEFAULT moves. Do not delete opencode-go rows, sections or the opencode-go route; only stop calling it the default and stop using it in the canonical default command.
- Example commands that show the skill default dispatch on OpenCode 1 (`--model opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash`) change to `--model llmgateway/deepseek-v4.1-flash`. Commands whose point is the opencode-go provider itself (a provider check like `opencode models opencode-go`, a variant-range test of opencode-go) keep it.
- Never edit lines inside `changelog/` or `benchmark/`, and never edit a line starting `Coverage note (2026-04-26):` (dated records).

